From: telegram-custom <telegram-custom@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 00:02:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Eight accounts without Premium

Stock Telegram allows 3 logged-in accounts, 4 with Premium. This raises
the slot count to 8 for everyone:

- UserConfig: MAX_ACCOUNT_COUNT 4 -> 8 and MAX_ACCOUNT_DEFAULT_COUNT
  3 -> 8. The "Add account" gate (UserInfoActivity, MainTabsActivity,
  LogoutActivity) subtracts MAX - DEFAULT free slots for non-Premium
  users, which is now 0, so all 8 slots are free; the three call sites
  are untouched. getMaxAccountCount() (display only, was 5/3) returns
  the constant.
- UserInfoActivity: the "Subscribe to Premium to use up to N accounts"
  footer under the account list shows only while Premium still adds
  slots, which it no longer does.
- NotificationsController: the per-account summary notification id was
  account + 1. For slots 4-7 that is 5-8, and 5 and 6 are the fixed ids
  of the music player / import and live-location service notifications,
  so slots 4-7 use 1000 + account instead. Slots 0-3 keep 1-4.
- Native tgnet: Defines.h MAX_ACCOUNT_COUNT 5 -> 8 (sizes jniEnv[] and
  the setJava() delegate loop) and ConnectionsManager::getInstance()
  gets cases 5-7, with default now on 7. Without this, Java slots 5-7
  would silently share native instance 4: one connection and one
  tgnet.dat for several accounts.

Existing slots 0-3 keep their indices, so their data (userconfing /
userconfig1..3 prefs, account1..3 dirs, tgnet.dat) is unchanged. New
slots get userconfig4..7 and files/account4..7 by the same string
pattern. Every slot, logged in or not, gets its controllers and a
native ConnectionsManager (one network thread) at app start, so the
four extra slots cost some memory and startup time even when empty.
